(7815609, 1305881, 67444, '<td valign="top">
Congratulations!
<br/>
<br/>Re that lone "3": I know beauty is subjective, and everyone responds to images differently. Still, imo, considering both the subject and the technical quality, this does not seem to fall within the 3/10 range of the rubric. I also remember that in the early years of DPC, there was a line under “Challenge Voting” that said something that any attempts to alter the point totals in any way for any photograph will result in immediate loss of account and a ban from the site (quite harsh imo lol). I am not sure whether this situation would fall under that, so I do not want to assume.
<br/>
<br/>One of the hardest things about being an artist, whether a singer, painter, poet or a photographer, is finding a style so uniquely yours that people can recognize your work without any identifying marks/signature [(apologies in advance, but off the top of my head, the ones I can think of right now are <img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=14386" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">librodo</a>, <img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=114969" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">gyaban</a>, <img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_N.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_N.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=113156" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">jagar</a>, <img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=103142" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">vawendy</a>, <img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=67145" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">roz</a>). To me, that is one of the “I’ve made it” moments in the competitive scene (so, congratulations, Anita). But I also think it can be a double-edged sword.
<br/>
<br/>I hope that one day I find my own style too</td>', 'Congratulations!

Re that lone "3": I know beauty is subjective, and everyone responds to images differently. Still, imo, considering both the subject and the technical quality, this does not seem to fall within the 3/10 range of the rubric. I also remember that in the early years of DPC, there was a line under “Challenge Voting” that said something that any attempts to alter the point totals in any way for any photograph will result in immediate loss of account and a ban from the site (quite harsh imo lol). I am not sure whether this situation would fall under that, so I do not want to assume.

One of the hardest things about being an artist, whether a singer, painter, poet or a photographer, is finding a style so uniquely yours that people can recognize your work without any identifying marks/signature [(apologies in advance, but off the top of my head, the ones I can think of right now are  librodo,  gyaban,  jagar,  vawendy,  roz). To me, that is one of the “I’ve made it” moments in the competitive scene (so, congratulations, Anita). But I also think it can be a double-edged sword.

I hope that one day I find my own style too', '2026-04-22 08:54:41.000000', NULL, 0),
